# Business logic source of truth

- Before changing domain logic, roles, flows, permissions, or provider-scoped resources, read `docs/business-logic.md`.
- For access-control details, also read `frontend/docs/roles-and-permissions.md`.
- Treat `docs/business-logic.md` as the primary product source of truth unless the user explicitly overrides it.
- Do not invent new roles, statuses, or business entities unless they are added to the spec first.
- Any provider-owned resource must be scoped by `providerId`.
- Do not trust client-supplied `providerId` for protected create/update/delete flows.
- Do not rely on UI-only permission checks; enforce access on the server.
- Do not treat placeholder UI sections as fully implemented product features.
- If implementation and spec diverge, prefer updating the spec or asking the user before expanding the domain model.
